  "id": "DrugBank_DB00405 - MONDO_grouped_11786_5324_24332",
  "verbalization": "Dexbrompheniramine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Allergic Rhinitis through a multi-step mechanism involving the treatment of Urticaria and Vasomotor Rhinitis. The drug is associated with Urticaria, which in turn is linked to both Bilastine and Rupatadine, both of which are indicated for Allergic Rhinitis. This suggests a potential pathway where Dexbrompheniramine may modulate inflammatory responses through the suppression of allergic reactions, possibly by inhibiting histamine release or other mediators involved in allergic inflammation. The evidence from the three paths indicates a consistent association between Dexbrompheniramine and Allergic Rhinitis, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple intermediate diseases supports the hypothesis that Dexbrompheniramine may exert a therapeutic effect on allergic rhinitis through a mechanism that involves the modulation of inflammatory pathways, though further experimental validation is required to confirm this.",
